with things we didn't even

00:44:12.950 --> 00:44:13.950
think about doing before

00:44:13.950 --> 00:44:16.030
because it was just it was unfeasible

00:44:16.030 --> 00:44:18.190
that can now be done with AI.

00:44:18.190 --> 00:44:19.270
An example is

00:44:19.270 --> 00:44:20.390
I'm on an advisory board

00:44:20.390 --> 00:44:21.270
for a couple of companies

00:44:21.270 --> 00:44:22.910
that are using agentic AI

00:44:22.910 --> 00:44:24.910
to solve very specific problems.

00:44:25.230 --> 00:44:26.310
And this is a much better

00:44:26.310 --> 00:44:27.950
like I look at GPT

00:44:27.950 --> 00:44:29.990
or all these things is like

00:44:29.990 --> 00:44:31.430
AI is the average of the Internet.

00:44:31.430 --> 00:44:32.550
They're trained on everything.

00:44:32.550 --> 00:44:33.830
So they give you a nice little average.

00:44:33.830 --> 00:44:34.630
They're good.

00:44:34.630 --> 00:44:35.710
People use.

00:44:35.710 --> 00:44:36.630
I think people use chat

00:44:36.630 --> 00:44:38.710
GPT very inefficiently a lot.

00:44:38.710 --> 00:44:40.550
It's just it's a search engine

00:44:40.550 --> 00:44:41.670
where you can use real text

00:44:41.670 --> 00:44:43.230
and it guesses for you.

00:44:43.230 --> 00:44:44.390
But I think with a real

00:44:44.390 --> 00:44:45.910
interesting things happen

00:44:45.910 --> 00:44:48.940
when you take AI agents

00:44:48.940 --> 00:44:50.060
for agentic AI

00:44:50.060 --> 00:44:52.940
and train them on specific problems

00:44:52.940 --> 00:44:55.380
and use them to solve problems

00:44:55.380 --> 00:44:57.700
that were unsolvable before.

00:44:57.700 --> 00:45:00.060
You know, the canonical example is

00:45:00.060 --> 00:45:01.300
pick your logging system.

00:45:01.300 --> 00:45:03.020
People always log way too much

00:45:03.020 --> 00:45:04.140
and people and humans go

00:45:04.140 --> 00:45:05.140
and try and find that out.

00:45:05.140 --> 00:45:06.220
Or, you know, five years ago,

00:45:06.220 --> 00:45:07.140
they use ML to try

00:45:07.140 --> 00:45:09.220
and find some insights.

00:45:09.220 --> 00:45:11.060
Having these AI agents

00:45:11.060 --> 00:45:13.460
is a way to solve that problem.

00:45:13.460 --> 00:45:14.540
There are some

00:45:14.540 --> 00:45:16.300
there are some opportunities

00:45:16.300 --> 00:45:18.500
for testing tools as well.

00:45:18.500 --> 00:45:19.500
But if you get that agent

00:45:19.500 --> 00:45:21.540
to act like a specific kind of tester

00:45:21.540 --> 00:45:23.260
trained on very specific

00:45:23.260 --> 00:45:24.420
curated information

00:45:24.420 --> 00:45:26.380
versus the average of,

00:45:26.380 --> 00:45:27.860
you know, 10,000 books on testing,

00:45:27.860 --> 00:45:29.340
which all contradict each other.

00:45:29.340 --> 00:45:30.020
There's a story I tell.

00:45:30.020 --> 00:45:30.740
I read my first book

00:45:30.740 --> 00:45:31.460
on software testing.

00:45:31.460 --> 00:45:32.540
I thought I knew a lot.

00:45:32.540 --> 00:45:33.620
I read my second testing.

00:45:33.620 --> 00:45:34.580
I was confused.

00:45:34.580 --> 00:45:35.740
And my third book,

00:45:35.740 --> 00:45:37.380
I began to see the conflicts

00:45:37.380 --> 00:45:38.740
in ideas, ideologies

00:45:38.740 --> 00:45:40.580
and philosophies and for my own opinions.

00:45:40.580 --> 00:45:42.900
I think the the LLMs

00:45:42.900 --> 00:45:43.780
have that same problem

00:45:43.780 --> 00:45:44.700
if you don't curate those.

00:45:44.700 --> 00:45:45.700
If you're trying to solve

00:45:45.700 --> 00:45:46.820
a very specific problem

00:45:46.820 --> 00:45:49.060
and you can train your AI

00:45:49.060 --> 00:45:51.140
on an LLM based on a large

00:45:51.140 --> 00:45:52.540
and it's a large set of data.

00:45:52.540 --> 00:45:54.620
So it's not just ML,

00:45:54.620 --> 00:45:56.900
but you're doing that

00:45:56.900 --> 00:45:58.100
to solve a specific problem

00:45:58.100 --> 00:46:00.300
using curated data to train that model.

00:46:00.300 --> 00:46:01.860
There's some really interesting problems

00:46:01.860 --> 00:46:02.660
that can be solved.

00:46:02.660 --> 00:46:04.940
And those are just the easy ones.

00:46:04.940 --> 00:46:06.740
I have to believe

00:46:06.740 --> 00:46:08.100
that there are problems

00:46:08.100 --> 00:46:09.060
that we have ignored

00:46:09.060 --> 00:46:10.100
or haven't even thought about

00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:11.900
because they've been deemed impossible

00:46:11.900 --> 00:46:13.940
that can be solved through

00:46:13.940 --> 00:46:15.220
agentic AI or something,

00:46:15.220 --> 00:46:17.500
something gen AI equivalent

00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:19.140
that we just haven't done yet

00:46:19.140 --> 00:46:22.580
because I guess my main point is

00:46:22.580 --> 00:46:23.580
you're absolutely right

00:46:23.580 --> 00:46:25.500
that companies don't need as many people

00:46:25.500 --> 00:46:26.820
because they're more productive.

00:46:26.820 --> 00:46:29.060
I cannot believe that we've invented

00:46:29.060 --> 00:46:30.380
everything we can in software

00:46:30.380 --> 00:46:31.220
and there aren't jobs

00:46:31.220 --> 00:46:32.420
for people to go invent those

